# Cloudflare Pages reads this file. Three kinds of rule live here: rewrites that
# keep a published URL working after the file behind it moved, and 301s for
# pages and files that were retired or renamed.

# ---- moved in the repo, not on the web ----------------------------------
# The pages live under pages/ now, and the icons and documents under files/.
# A 200 is a rewrite, not a redirect: the address bar keeps the short URL and
# Cloudflare serves the file from its new path.
#
# Every target here is a directory, never a path ending in index.html. Pages
# canonicalises a URL that names index.html (and one that ends .html) by
# redirecting to the directory, and it does that to the target of a rewrite as
# well, which turns the rewrite into a visible 307 and leaks the long path into
# the address bar. A directory is already canonical, so it is served as-is.
# The splat covers the bare form too: /tiny with an empty splat lands on the
# same directory.
/crucible        /pages/projects/crucible/        200
/crucible/*      /pages/projects/crucible/:splat  200

/tiny            /pages/projects/tiny/            200
/tiny/*          /pages/projects/tiny/:splat      200

/cosmos          /pages/projects/cosmos/          200
/cosmos/*        /pages/projects/cosmos/:splat    200

/misc            /pages/misc/                     200
/misc/*          /pages/misc/:splat               200

# The old file URLs. Every page here points at the new paths already; these are
# for links that left the site: the resume URL in particular is on a CV and in
# applications, and the preview image is cached by anything that has scraped a
# link to the site.
/favicon.svg                               /files/images/favicon.svg                  301
/favicon.png                               /files/images/favicon.png                  301
/og.png                                    /files/images/og.png                       301
/files/matthew-saunders-resume.pdf         /files/docs/matthew-saunders-resume.pdf    301
/files/fundamentals-of-remote-sensing.pdf  /files/docs/fundamentals-of-remote-sensing.pdf  301

# ---- retired pages -------------------------------------------------------
# The two pages folded into /misc/. Both were live and indexed, so they redirect
# rather than 404.
/hobbies/*  /misc/  301
/gallery/*  /misc/  301

# The projects are portfolio entries on the About page now, linking to their own
# pages; nothing lives under /projects/ any more. The index and all three
# writeups were live and indexed, so the whole tree redirects home.
/projects/*  /  301
/projects  /  301
